MVVM-lite (Model–View–ViewModel, simplified):

A design pattern where:

Model = your core domain/game state (saskan.core, engine).

View = the UI widgets (Qt forms, PyGame canvas).

ViewModel = a mediator object that exposes just the data and commands the View needs, in a UI-friendly form (strings, lists, events).
“Lite” = you don’t implement the full WPF-style data binding framework — just thin viewmodels to keep UI code clean and testable.
